Z||000000||bilbo||05-11-2001||09:54 AM||||Does anyone know if you can take the original seat upholstry off the seats without ripping or cutting?????  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||RacinRob||05-11-2001||10:09 AM||||yes you can but it is a little tricky and there are two hog rings you have to take off the back of the seat.  They just unzip, put some WD40 on the zippers since they have been used in a while.<BR>look here for more info <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by RacinRob (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-11-2001||10:13 AM||||You can remove all the seat covers without damaging them. Just go slowly. I was able to remove mine without damage when I went to the leather seats.||||reg||1
